Problem Statement
Develop a C++ program to represent airport facilities as vertices and possible ground connections as weighted edges. Apply Prim’s algorithm to connect the facilities with minimum total cost. Display the selected connections and the total cost.
2. Modified Problem Statement
Modify the C++ program to implement the following operations:
A. Update an edge weight and apply Prim’s algorithm again to find the minimum spanning tree.
B. Display every selected edge with its weight and the running total cost.
C. Detect a disconnected graph and report whether a minimum spanning tree can be formed.
